WEBVTT

01:04.189 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:15.742 --> 01:20.121
How could he think of running away
after blaming his friend for everything?

01:21.790 --> 01:26.211
He planned to take everything and run.
That's why he opened the pawnshop.

01:26.711 --> 01:29.464
You think I didn't like him
'cause he was bottom of the class?

01:29.547 --> 01:33.718
When he was ten, he came to our house
and stole your dad's washer fluid.

01:33.802 --> 01:34.719
My washer fluid?

01:35.386 --> 01:37.138
-Why would he?
-God knows why.

01:37.222 --> 01:39.891
He just stole
whatever he could get his hands on.

01:39.974 --> 01:41.351
He came with empty pockets,

01:41.434 --> 01:43.561
but every time he said goodbye and left,

01:43.645 --> 01:45.730
his pockets were always so stuffed!

01:45.814 --> 01:50.026
What's the point of saying that?
The issue now is the buncheong stoneware.

01:50.110 --> 01:51.986
That woman is such a liar,

01:52.070 --> 01:55.615
claiming it was appraised for 70 million
on Authentic Masterpieces.

01:56.241 --> 01:57.075
Seventy…

01:58.159 --> 01:59.452
Seventy million won?

01:59.536 --> 02:02.247
Why leave her buncheong stoneware
at a tiny pawnshop?

02:02.831 --> 02:03.873
Oh my goodness.

02:04.833 --> 02:07.752
Why did you do it? Why?

02:07.836 --> 02:11.548
Why did it have to be with Cheol-yong?
And why a pawnshop?

02:11.631 --> 02:14.300
Is it a pawnshop's fault?
Blame the IMF crisis.

02:14.384 --> 02:17.262
They're handing out credit cards
and cash advances,

02:17.345 --> 02:19.556
so who the hell would come to a pawnshop?

02:19.639 --> 02:23.226
That's not all. Gold collection.
That goddamn gold collection campaign!

02:23.309 --> 02:25.937
With the country throwing
a one-two punch at me, how can I--

02:26.020 --> 02:28.189
Should they not even collect gold
for your sake?

02:29.691 --> 02:33.486
You wanted to strike gold and look cool.
And now, none of this is your fault?

02:34.070 --> 02:36.698
You should live within your means.

02:36.781 --> 02:39.701
You took out a loan for the pawnshop.
That damn lucky strike!

02:39.784 --> 02:41.578
I did it so I wouldn't live like you.

02:41.661 --> 02:45.248
I hate the idea
of living within your means.

02:45.331 --> 02:48.334
You always reeked of cooling patches,
but what did you do for me?

02:48.418 --> 02:49.377
Yang Eun-myeong!

02:49.460 --> 02:52.964
What have you ever done for me?
You've always had your favorite.

02:53.047 --> 02:56.551
Be honest. Have you two ever told me
that I'm the best?

02:57.218 --> 03:01.431
To Geum-myeong, you always say,
"You do everything well."

03:02.098 --> 03:05.602
Did you ever say that to me?
Why do I always go on about money?

03:06.477 --> 03:08.479
What else can I beat Geum-myeong in?

03:09.105 --> 03:10.356
I did it for you to notice.

03:10.440 --> 03:12.859
Just so you'd look at me. Okay?

03:19.657 --> 03:22.285
Why can't I have a birthday party?

03:22.368 --> 03:25.038
You threw one for Geum-myeong.
What about me?

03:25.705 --> 03:26.664
Eun-myeong.

03:27.165 --> 03:27.999
I'm sorry.

03:28.499 --> 03:32.378
I just have such a bad headache right now.

03:33.379 --> 03:34.714
Get up.

03:34.797 --> 03:36.216
Make me rice cakes!

03:36.299 --> 03:37.884
I want rice cakes too!

03:38.593 --> 03:39.761
Come here, Eun-myeong!

03:45.016 --> 03:48.645
Your brother passed away
three days after your birthday.

03:48.728 --> 03:50.563
Just accept living without a birthday.

03:50.647 --> 03:53.858
You're the eldest son
who should soothe your parents.

03:53.942 --> 03:56.027
You have to live
for you and your brother now.

03:56.110 --> 03:58.821
Otherwise, your mother can't go on.

03:58.905 --> 04:01.574
But that's not fair!

04:02.283 --> 04:05.328
I don't want to!

04:05.828 --> 04:09.165
I don't want to!

04:09.916 --> 04:11.251
Eun-myeong, come out here.

04:13.586 --> 04:15.004
YANG GEUM-MYEONG
DAILY SCHEDULE

04:18.174 --> 04:20.385
What in the world are you drawing?

04:20.468 --> 04:21.511
Just watch.

04:21.594 --> 04:23.012
YANG EUN-MYEONG
SPELLING TEST

04:25.556 --> 04:28.810
Mom and Dad have a huge hole
in their hearts because of Dong-myeong.

04:28.893 --> 04:30.395
How can anyone live like that?

04:33.189 --> 04:36.192
It needs to be filled for them to live.
So what should we do?

04:36.776 --> 04:38.403
Stop asking me and just say it.

04:38.903 --> 04:42.115
You get a "Well done" stamp
for doing your homework well, right?

04:43.157 --> 04:43.992
Look at this.

04:45.910 --> 04:48.746
We have to stamp it countless times
with a tiny stamp.

04:49.622 --> 04:52.166
We have to keep stamping
every day to fill it up.

04:55.420 --> 04:56.504
So they can go on.

04:58.256 --> 04:59.090
You understand?

04:59.716 --> 05:02.635
You're the know-it-all.
What am I supposed to do?

05:03.428 --> 05:04.429
"Know-it-all"?

05:06.723 --> 05:08.725
YANG GWAN-SIK

05:09.309 --> 05:11.519
Look at this. Look at what I got.

05:14.856 --> 05:17.317
Wow. It went up by ten.

05:18.818 --> 05:20.528
I got one wrong on home economics.

05:21.029 --> 05:22.905
The teacher made the test question weird.

05:24.073 --> 05:26.576
One? One question out of all subjects?

05:46.804 --> 05:47.638
What am I, a dog?

05:48.222 --> 05:49.724
I only get leftovers?

05:50.224 --> 05:53.478
Dad and your sister
have to take packed lunches.

05:54.729 --> 05:56.773
I want more pork cutlets.
Fry me a new one.

05:57.398 --> 05:59.692
Your sister's picky about food
and has exams.

06:00.568 --> 06:02.612
And Dad's work is very tiring.

06:07.158 --> 06:09.660
What's wrong with you?

06:09.744 --> 06:11.412
Have you hit puberty already?

06:18.711 --> 06:19.921
Goodness.

06:20.421 --> 06:24.634
Kang Ho-dong's mom must have no regrets.

06:24.717 --> 06:27.929
If a mother had a son
who brought home a golden calf,

06:29.430 --> 06:30.681
what's left to wish for?

06:30.765 --> 06:34.769
A golden calf is all you need?
You'd want nothing else if you had one?

06:36.771 --> 06:38.606
Mom, just follow me.

06:38.689 --> 06:41.692
If you stay by my side,
the least you'll get is a golden calf.

06:41.776 --> 06:43.277
I'm gonna buy you a Mercedes.

06:46.864 --> 06:51.452
I'll stop Dad from sailing his boat
and make you quit your street stall.

06:51.536 --> 06:54.288
It will be me, not Geum-myeong!

06:54.372 --> 06:57.917
When's that ever gonna happen?

06:58.000 --> 07:02.630
If you won a golden calf for me,

07:03.131 --> 07:07.176
I could just go all around Hallasan
dancing and bragging.

07:07.260 --> 07:10.721
Goodness. You're such a windbag!

07:11.514 --> 07:13.141
Where did you get that from?

07:14.600 --> 07:19.605
Your sister just got things done
without saying a word.

07:30.366 --> 07:35.246
Carelessly-spoken dry words
made Eun-myeong grow up hungry.

07:36.706 --> 07:38.374
Favoritism is really unfair.

07:39.584 --> 07:41.627
It's better not to love at all.

07:41.711 --> 07:44.589
Giving less love is so unfair.

07:45.673 --> 07:47.341
It stops a child from growing.

07:48.217 --> 07:50.761
Mom's long-standing fear had come true.

07:55.766 --> 07:56.851
Aren't you scared?

07:59.061 --> 08:00.229
Of course I am.

08:00.980 --> 08:02.565
I still can't believe it.

08:04.901 --> 08:07.320
How is this thing going to come out of me?

08:09.614 --> 08:10.448
But

08:11.532 --> 08:13.493
what's scarier than giving birth

08:14.410 --> 08:16.245
is what happens afterward.

08:18.831 --> 08:19.665
Why's that?

08:21.375 --> 08:22.210
Well,

08:22.919 --> 08:25.922
they say experience is the best teacher,

08:26.464 --> 08:27.924
but I don't know much.

08:29.509 --> 08:31.344
I haven't had much to learn from.

08:33.429 --> 08:35.306
Worried you won't know how to be a mom?

08:35.890 --> 08:38.267
What do I do for them
when they hit puberty?

08:39.477 --> 08:41.354
What if they're a bit of a punk?

08:42.021 --> 08:43.523
Are you that worried about it?

08:45.775 --> 08:47.485
To be honest, what I fear the most…

08:51.113 --> 08:54.450
is that I might hurt them
because I don't know how to be a mom.

08:55.076 --> 08:56.327
That scares me the most.

08:57.328 --> 09:01.374
This tiny thing is coming into the world,
trusting only me.

09:01.999 --> 09:04.502
I can't scar the baby's life.

09:08.172 --> 09:09.674
You won't scar their life.

09:11.634 --> 09:14.762
You couldn't even if you wanted to.

09:16.806 --> 09:18.558
The truth is…

09:20.726 --> 09:22.979
I want to be a really good mom.

09:24.313 --> 09:25.481
A really good one!

09:28.568 --> 09:30.778
Do you know why I named my son Che-il?

09:31.320 --> 09:33.739
It means "number one,"
something I've never been.

09:35.533 --> 09:36.534
Never.

09:38.244 --> 09:40.121
That's how you two raised me.

09:49.380 --> 09:52.341
What about your mom?
You think she was ever number one?

09:52.425 --> 09:57.471
That pork cutlet you were so hung up on.
How many do you think your mom got to eat?

09:58.264 --> 09:59.098
Go.

09:59.181 --> 10:01.017
-You darned…
-Step out for a bit.

10:01.100 --> 10:03.894
You darned… foolish idiot.

10:03.978 --> 10:05.354
Don't get me out of here.

10:05.438 --> 10:09.150
Your darned, ungrateful son
will pay his debt using his own back.

10:10.109 --> 10:12.320
Have it your way! What an honorable son!

10:15.072 --> 10:16.949
Father.

10:17.450 --> 10:19.118
Dad!

10:19.744 --> 10:20.661
Kick her out.

10:22.079 --> 10:23.456
Kick her out!

10:23.539 --> 10:25.249
Give me some money.

10:25.333 --> 10:27.376
Please give me some money!

10:27.460 --> 10:29.003
Do I owe you money or something?

10:29.086 --> 10:30.963
I know there's my share.

10:31.047 --> 10:33.174
Think of it
as giving me my inheritance now!

10:33.257 --> 10:34.508
Am I already dead to you?

10:36.344 --> 10:37.678
What am I supposed to do?

10:38.596 --> 10:40.264
You want me to be a prisoner's wife?

10:40.890 --> 10:42.767
You want Che-il to be a criminal's son?

10:42.850 --> 10:46.812
Tell them to catch the real criminal.
If he's innocent, why pay for him?

10:49.523 --> 10:52.943
Eun-myeong really didn't do
anything wrong!

10:53.486 --> 10:56.530
He did it so we could live a better life!

10:56.614 --> 10:58.240
If he's innocent, he'll get out.

11:03.954 --> 11:05.331
So money comes before me?

11:05.414 --> 11:07.667
Of course it does. A hundred times over.

11:08.876 --> 11:11.462
Have you ever done anything
to be a good daughter?

11:14.006 --> 11:17.885
Did you ever make me a boat captain
or chief of the co-op?

11:17.968 --> 11:21.055
Money does it all.
It's the real filial duty!

11:22.264 --> 11:24.850
You think being a child
is some kind of privilege?

11:25.351 --> 11:29.730
I don't need a child
who never listens to me either!

11:33.776 --> 11:36.821
Dad, do you know
what I envy most about my sister-in-law?

11:37.738 --> 11:39.365
Having a father like hers.

11:40.324 --> 11:44.078
With my fate, even if I were reborn,
I could never have a dad like hers.

11:45.496 --> 11:47.957
She has a heart
like a fancy car with a big engine.

11:49.250 --> 11:51.252
But your daughter's
not even worth a wagon.

12:00.761 --> 12:02.304
Yeah, same here!

12:03.556 --> 12:06.392
It's only 70 million.
Is it such a big deal?

12:08.644 --> 12:10.271
"Only 70 million"?

12:10.980 --> 12:14.233
Hey, have you even earned 100 won?

12:15.776 --> 12:17.528
Respect, gratitude,

12:18.320 --> 12:20.698
and affection for one's parents.

12:21.949 --> 12:25.077
Even ten billion wouldn't be enough
to buy these things.

12:26.495 --> 12:28.414
No money can pull out

12:30.124 --> 12:32.084
the peg you drive into your child's heart.

12:32.168 --> 12:34.086
You think you're the only one who thinks?

12:34.170 --> 12:38.466
I think too. I think way ahead of you!

12:38.549 --> 12:41.051
The ship you treasure
more than your own child

12:41.552 --> 12:43.846
got its price tag
right after it was made, right?

12:43.929 --> 12:48.642
But a person's worth
is only determined after they die.

12:50.394 --> 12:53.522
Starting tonight,
you can spend sleepless nights

12:54.398 --> 12:57.693
in fear of how much your life
will truly be worth.

13:03.157 --> 13:04.492
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

13:06.911 --> 13:07.745
CHEOL-YONG SALON

13:07.828 --> 13:09.705
Go ahead and take my life.

13:11.582 --> 13:14.418
Even if you beat me to death,
I don't know where Cheol-yong is.

13:14.502 --> 13:16.921
You won't find a single cent
even if you cut me open.

13:17.004 --> 13:19.381
That buncheong was worth 70 million won!

13:19.465 --> 13:23.427
Why should her son pay
for what your son ran off with?

13:23.511 --> 13:25.805
My son is also a victim in a way.

13:25.888 --> 13:27.932
Look at her running her damn mouth!

13:28.015 --> 13:33.103
My good kid trusted a snake
and got bitten.

13:33.604 --> 13:36.398
You can tell just by looking
at Eun-myeong's nasty hairstyle.

13:36.482 --> 13:38.776
Who's been messing with his hair
all those years?

13:38.859 --> 13:41.278
His bad influence rubbed off on my son.

13:41.362 --> 13:43.989
He's gone and ruined my son's future too.

13:45.032 --> 13:47.243
Ae-sun, aren't you going to say anything?

13:47.868 --> 13:49.787
We can't fight for you forever!

13:52.790 --> 13:55.251
You're colluding with him, aren't you?

13:56.627 --> 13:59.755
If you find out where my son is,
please let me know.

13:59.839 --> 14:03.759
I have to change the name of the shop
thanks to my wonderful son.

14:08.389 --> 14:11.016
Did Cheol-yong sell
the buncheong stoneware

14:12.685 --> 14:15.688
to buy you this television
and that gold ring?

14:17.231 --> 14:18.232
Got any evidence?

14:19.525 --> 14:20.568
Bring me the evidence.

14:20.651 --> 14:22.570
Now that I see you like this,

14:22.653 --> 14:24.947
I get why Cheol-yong turned out
so horribly!

14:25.030 --> 14:27.199
Did Eun-myeong end up in prison

14:27.283 --> 14:30.244
because he takes after
his high-school-dropout mom?

14:31.120 --> 14:33.163
He just turned out as he was meant to.

14:39.295 --> 14:40.838
What the hell?

14:41.964 --> 14:43.424
You pea-brained bitch!

14:43.507 --> 14:44.717
Let go now!

14:44.800 --> 14:47.720
There are three of us! Damn you!

14:57.146 --> 14:59.690
-Chip in!
-Let go first!

14:59.773 --> 15:00.983
You chip in too!

15:01.066 --> 15:04.653
If you make someone cry blood,
at least act like you'll pay it back!

15:05.446 --> 15:08.532
Ae-sun, why don't you
let her go first and…

15:09.241 --> 15:13.037
When your son gets taken away,
you go into a blind rage!

15:13.120 --> 15:15.789
I don't care about anything right now!

15:15.873 --> 15:16.707
Got it?

15:19.209 --> 15:20.794
She's indeed Gwang-rye's daughter.

15:31.096 --> 15:35.017
Mom grabbed someone by the hair
for the first time in her life.

15:40.356 --> 15:42.191
You'd lose to her now.

15:42.983 --> 15:44.902
That was some technique, huh?

15:45.486 --> 15:49.073
She grabbed her hair and twisted her body,
like some ssireum technique.

15:49.782 --> 15:51.909
They say moms grow stronger over time

15:52.493 --> 15:54.328
while dads grow more fragile.

15:55.871 --> 15:57.456
-That Steelheart?
-Yeah.

15:59.917 --> 16:03.712
Dad also went to do something
for the first time in his life.

16:13.806 --> 16:17.643
Didn't I tell you to invest in a place
while they were building in Seogwipo?

16:18.686 --> 16:21.730
Your son was always going on
about lucky strikes.

16:23.983 --> 16:25.651
Stay and hang out for a bit.

16:26.151 --> 16:28.654
Goddamn IMF crisis. Seriously.

16:29.822 --> 16:31.991
I have to do my own deliveries these days.

16:32.074 --> 16:33.367
-Hey!
-Sir.

16:34.076 --> 16:34.994
Could you maybe

16:36.161 --> 16:37.121
lend me…

16:40.124 --> 16:42.001
You've known me for a long time.

16:42.084 --> 16:43.627
I never take a day off.

16:43.711 --> 16:46.296
I'll catch all the fish in the sea
so that I can--

16:46.380 --> 16:48.674
Captain Yang, you're not young anymore.

16:48.757 --> 16:53.137
Your knees get so sore in bad weather,
you can't even pull in your nets alone.

16:53.220 --> 16:54.096
Sir.

16:54.179 --> 16:56.348
Everyone knows me
as a great fisherman, and--

16:56.432 --> 16:58.684
The world has changed.

16:59.810 --> 17:03.981
They're sweeping up fish
with trawlers the size of a house.

17:04.064 --> 17:08.235
But you're still old-fashioned,
letting all the small, borderline fish go.

17:08.318 --> 17:11.613
You're the best at following spawning
and closed fishing seasons in Jeju.

17:11.697 --> 17:15.117
Who on earth makes money like that?
Have you made a lot, Captain Yang?

17:16.076 --> 17:16.910
Sir.

17:18.537 --> 17:19.621
I'll pay you back.

17:19.705 --> 17:22.249
I'll pay you back,
be it with fish or my body.

17:22.332 --> 17:24.877
Good grief, just get the idea already!

17:24.960 --> 17:27.421
You're really making me uncomfortable.

17:27.504 --> 17:29.173
Just go! Leave.

17:29.965 --> 17:32.926
The whole port is avoiding you,
Captain Yang.

17:34.344 --> 17:38.682
How did such an upstanding, reserved man
end up like that?

17:39.391 --> 17:41.518
Parents bear the burden of their kids.

17:43.729 --> 17:46.732
My son just turned 26.

17:49.985 --> 17:51.862
To me, he's like my crooked finger.

17:52.613 --> 17:53.447
and I…

17:54.239 --> 17:55.449
I…

17:57.868 --> 17:59.661
can't just give up and leave.

18:38.117 --> 18:39.952
CAR LIFE

18:46.542 --> 18:51.338
FISHING LOG

18:59.721 --> 19:05.310
FISHING LOG

19:32.671 --> 19:34.298
AUGUST 15, EUN-MYEONG'S BIRTHDAY

19:34.381 --> 19:35.465
AUGUST 18, TYPHOON CARMEN

19:35.549 --> 19:39.887
Dad returned to sea after just three days,
even after sending Dong-myeong off.

19:42.973 --> 19:46.768
In the end, Dad sold 20 years of his life,

19:48.729 --> 19:53.358
which carries the three of us
and which he could never part with.

19:54.067 --> 19:55.861
He sold Geumeundong, his boat.

20:09.833 --> 20:13.462
M.F.L.

20:13.545 --> 20:16.215
Erase the moth. Why did you draw it here?

20:16.298 --> 20:17.257
It's a butterfly.

20:20.928 --> 20:22.638
Write a poem for me too.

20:23.138 --> 20:25.265
Titled "Yang Gwan-sik."

20:28.352 --> 20:29.478
Why would I?

20:43.075 --> 20:44.826
"M.F.L."

20:45.494 --> 20:48.622
by Oh Ae-sun from class 1-5
of Dodong Girls' High.

20:49.957 --> 20:53.418
When it's around, it's annoying
When it's not, I'm curious

20:53.502 --> 20:54.836
Why read it so many times?

20:54.920 --> 20:58.840
When I tease it, it's fine
When others do, I get mad

21:00.884 --> 21:04.972
With eyes open, I pretend not to see
With eyes closed, its image comes to me

21:05.055 --> 21:08.225
Unnoticed, like the sea I see every day

21:08.308 --> 21:11.478
Yet without it,
I'm alone in the vast world

21:12.479 --> 21:15.148
Like candy hidden in my mouth

21:15.732 --> 21:17.943
Its sweetness overflows all around

21:19.111 --> 21:20.237
Is this it

21:21.571 --> 21:22.990
Is this it

21:23.991 --> 21:25.617
Is that why

21:26.451 --> 21:28.870
My heart stays in spring every day

21:32.207 --> 21:34.293
I told you to read it at home, didn't I?

21:46.847 --> 21:47.681
My first love.

21:49.933 --> 21:51.560
It means "My First Love," right?

21:52.144 --> 21:53.312
I know it does.

21:54.688 --> 21:57.149
Who said it was you? Who said so?

22:01.945 --> 22:03.113
Hey!

22:03.196 --> 22:06.241
You think just because we did it once,
you can keep doing it?

22:06.742 --> 22:08.076
-God.
-I can't?

22:10.954 --> 22:11.997
I can't do that?

22:16.543 --> 22:17.794
No questions!

22:18.754 --> 22:20.630
No more questions from you.

22:49.451 --> 22:51.161
"Spring every day," my foot.

22:52.579 --> 22:53.955
It's not spring at all.

22:56.291 --> 22:58.043
It's not spring at all.

23:02.839 --> 23:07.969
The boy's hands now made
the rustling sounds of winter branches.

23:08.053 --> 23:09.721
-Yeah, this is our boat.
-Our boat.

23:09.805 --> 23:11.098
Daddy's boat.

23:11.181 --> 23:12.015
Daddy's boat.

23:13.100 --> 23:14.851
-Hello.
-Were you inside?

23:15.644 --> 23:17.437
You'll wear out the boat by staring.

23:18.438 --> 23:20.941
My wife kept saying
she wanted to see our boat again.

23:21.024 --> 23:22.692
You said you wanted to see it too.

23:22.776 --> 23:23.860
No, I didn't.

23:27.739 --> 23:28.990
Daddy!

23:30.033 --> 23:31.618
-Daddy!
-Daddy!

23:32.452 --> 23:33.870
Hi.

23:33.954 --> 23:36.623
-Daddy!
-Daddy!

23:36.706 --> 23:38.250
-Did you catch a lot?
-Daddy!

23:38.333 --> 23:41.503
-Daddy! Hurry!
-Daddy!

23:44.423 --> 23:46.049
Have you decided on the boat name?

23:46.133 --> 23:48.885
You'll feel more fond of it
after you've named it.

23:49.719 --> 23:50.637
Well,

23:51.430 --> 23:52.431
it's Eunyeong.

23:53.723 --> 23:55.100
So you must be Eun-yeong.

23:55.183 --> 23:57.519
That's great. That's so great.

23:58.311 --> 24:00.063
Geum-myeong, Eun-myeong…

24:02.315 --> 24:04.484
and Dong-myeong grew up
thanks to this boat,

24:04.985 --> 24:06.403
so it will do the same for her.

24:06.486 --> 24:07.487
Thank you.

24:11.616 --> 24:12.451
Oh my.

24:16.496 --> 24:19.124
Wow, this is the boat's full history!

24:22.043 --> 24:25.922
These are from the last three years,
but if you need them…

24:26.006 --> 24:29.176
They are all old-fashioned,
so I don't know if they'll be helpful.

24:29.259 --> 24:30.594
FISHING LOG

24:30.677 --> 24:32.762
Is it really okay for me to have these?

24:32.846 --> 24:34.973
I don't think
I'll be a boat captain again.

24:37.017 --> 24:38.768
Well, we'd be really grateful. Truly.

24:39.394 --> 24:42.814
-Eun-yeong, say, "Thank you."
-Thank you, sir.

24:42.898 --> 24:45.358
Yes, thank you as well.

24:45.442 --> 24:46.818
Thank you.

24:47.402 --> 24:49.488
We were the only ones who didn't know.

24:49.988 --> 24:54.910
We never knew that the time Dad spent
at sea flew by in a heartbeat.

24:56.828 --> 25:00.040
At least you're out.
That's all that matters.

25:00.540 --> 25:02.709
Wait, I'm asking how you came up
with the money.

25:04.211 --> 25:05.795
-You sold the apartment?
-Let's go.

25:05.879 --> 25:06.880
You sold the boat?

25:10.759 --> 25:11.593
You did, right?

25:14.471 --> 25:15.388
Damn it.

25:23.813 --> 25:24.648
Don't cry.

25:24.731 --> 25:26.942
If you cry,
it will make your father cry too.

25:27.484 --> 25:29.694
He will cry countless times in his heart.

25:29.778 --> 25:31.530
Why would you sell the boat?

25:32.155 --> 25:34.616
Why would you do that for me? Damn it!

25:35.951 --> 25:39.246
We sold it because you're our number one!
Why wouldn't you be?

25:39.746 --> 25:43.333
A child may abandon sick parents,
but not the other way around.

25:43.416 --> 25:46.002
I hate this. Seriously.

25:48.129 --> 25:49.756
I really hate this!

25:51.091 --> 25:52.467
How could we not get you out?

25:52.968 --> 25:54.469
How could we leave you in there?

25:54.553 --> 25:56.555
A bucket that's always filled to the brim,

25:56.638 --> 25:59.140
no matter how many leaking holes it has.

25:59.766 --> 26:02.602
That's something Eun-myeong already had.

26:03.103 --> 26:05.814
You can resent me,
but don't do that to your father.

26:05.897 --> 26:09.025
Do you know
that your father eats five meals a day?

26:09.943 --> 26:12.904
His work was so hard
that he ate five meals a day all his life.

26:13.655 --> 26:16.241
He wouldn't have to live like that
if not for you guys.

26:17.409 --> 26:20.161
You can resent me,
but how can you resent him?

26:20.245 --> 26:21.079
Don't.

26:21.162 --> 26:22.414
If you do,

26:22.497 --> 26:25.041
your father's efforts
would've been in vain.

26:25.792 --> 26:27.043
So what's he doing now?

26:27.961 --> 26:31.423
If he doesn't catch fish,
what are you going to sell?

26:32.299 --> 26:34.509
You just worry about yourself, okay?

26:35.552 --> 26:36.803
Whatever I do,

26:37.971 --> 26:39.097
I do well now.

26:40.223 --> 26:42.017
The Literary Girl has changed.

26:49.107 --> 26:50.900
Not there, ma'am. Over here.

26:51.401 --> 26:52.944
Let me fillet your squid.

26:53.028 --> 26:55.530
See how fresh the squid is at this time.

26:57.532 --> 26:59.534
I'll fillet it perfectly for you.

26:59.618 --> 27:03.330
Only 2,000 won for 20
and 3,000 won for 40!

27:03.913 --> 27:05.874
Just bring them over to me.

27:05.957 --> 27:07.917
I'll fillet them for you!

27:08.001 --> 27:12.088
The girl who said 50 won for one cabbage
and 150 for three, no matter what,

27:12.172 --> 27:13.006
has changed.

27:13.089 --> 27:15.133
Hey! Are you the only one working here?

27:15.216 --> 27:17.552
If you keep slashing prices,
you will doom us all!

27:18.553 --> 27:21.473
Ma'am, you bought some squid?
Let me fillet them for you.

27:21.556 --> 27:23.099
I'll fillet them perfectly.

27:23.183 --> 27:26.102
Excuse me, ma'am.
What are you doing over there?

27:26.186 --> 27:27.103
I'm right here.

27:27.187 --> 27:29.439
Now you're stealing
other people's customers?

27:29.522 --> 27:31.524
You stole them, not me!

27:31.608 --> 27:34.653
Ma'am, who did you come here to see?

27:34.736 --> 27:38.156
Well, my mother-in-law told me
to go with the pretty lady.

27:38.823 --> 27:40.241
Then who would it be?

27:42.702 --> 27:44.412
Which one would it be?

27:45.538 --> 27:47.582
Hey! It could be me!

27:48.958 --> 27:53.380
The Literary Girl evolved
like Squirtle evolved into Blastoise.

27:53.463 --> 27:54.464
Come on.

27:54.547 --> 27:55.382
Goodness!

27:56.216 --> 27:59.552
All right. Let's fillet them.

28:07.185 --> 28:10.063
Wow, you have fast hands.

28:10.146 --> 28:13.858
When I was your age,
I couldn't do anything like this at all.

28:13.942 --> 28:15.860
You liar.

28:15.944 --> 28:18.071
How can a fisherman's wife
not fillet squid?

28:18.154 --> 28:21.074
My husband used to do it all for me.

28:21.157 --> 28:23.535
He didn't want me to get hurt
or be scared.

28:23.618 --> 28:25.370
Here's Oh Ae-sun's brag, verse one.

28:25.954 --> 28:30.375
My husband keeps begging me
not to do stuff like this.

28:30.458 --> 28:32.752
I just do it for fun.
Why waste time doing nothing?

28:32.836 --> 28:36.047
My husband's a boat captain, you see.

28:36.756 --> 28:38.383
Is he still a captain?

28:38.967 --> 28:41.469
Tell her what he does now. Go on.

28:41.553 --> 28:43.221
What does he do now?

28:45.515 --> 28:46.558
Hang on.

28:46.641 --> 28:49.686
It's my daughter.
She went to Seoul National University.

28:49.769 --> 28:52.355
She always calls me around mealtime.

28:53.940 --> 28:55.525
Hi, sweetie!

28:56.276 --> 28:58.445
You wanna make sure
that I'm eating every day?

28:59.028 --> 29:01.322
Here comes the second verse
of Ae-sun's brag.

29:01.406 --> 29:03.950
The children's phone calls
at every meal time

29:04.033 --> 29:05.910
were a source of power between them.

29:05.994 --> 29:09.956
Goodness, I don't need a checkup!

29:10.540 --> 29:12.667
No, don't bother.

29:13.877 --> 29:17.839
I love you too. Take care.

29:17.922 --> 29:22.510
Hey, I bet she didn't say she loves you.
You're just saying that, aren't you?

29:24.679 --> 29:28.725
The less she had, the more she bragged.

29:30.643 --> 29:32.937
Hey, there goes your boat captain.

29:33.021 --> 29:34.063
There he goes.

29:35.482 --> 29:38.693
I think that's how
Mom protected her own heart.

29:39.194 --> 29:41.905
Whatever. None of them ever get calls.

29:42.822 --> 29:47.577
It's only my kids who are always calling
to ask if I ate or what I ate.

29:48.453 --> 29:49.996
They're just jealous.

29:50.079 --> 29:52.999
You should change the candle right away
if the flame weakens.

29:54.000 --> 29:55.001
It will be cold.

29:58.463 --> 30:02.300
They don't even know the law
and think a holding cell is a prison.

30:02.383 --> 30:06.221
That damn Mi-suk clearly knows about it,
but she keeps asking,

30:06.304 --> 30:08.348
"Why aren't you talking about your son?"

30:08.431 --> 30:09.974
"What is he up to?"

30:10.058 --> 30:12.101
What nonsense. Damn bitch.

30:15.230 --> 30:16.981
No matter how much my life has shrunk,

30:17.565 --> 30:19.901
it's better than flirting
with others' men.

30:19.984 --> 30:21.444
Has your life shrunk?

30:23.863 --> 30:24.781
Of course not.

30:25.281 --> 30:26.741
I'm just saying.

30:27.867 --> 30:29.786
That's not what I meant.

30:29.869 --> 30:31.830
Everyone here is envious of me.

30:33.706 --> 30:36.042
Should I buy you a good cream?
An expensive one?

30:36.626 --> 30:37.627
Why?

30:38.378 --> 30:40.505
It looks like I put on blush.
Cute, isn't it?

30:41.214 --> 30:43.842
They call me the pretty one here.

30:49.305 --> 30:50.306
Oh man.

30:52.350 --> 30:53.685
Why is life like this…

30:54.227 --> 30:55.562
Why is it like this?

31:02.819 --> 31:04.153
What's wrong?

31:05.113 --> 31:06.406
Are you getting old?

31:08.199 --> 31:10.243
Why do you keep getting more tearful?

31:12.453 --> 31:14.831
How could I make you sit here like this?

31:15.373 --> 31:16.207
Oh man.

31:17.500 --> 31:19.627
I couldn't even fulfill
any of your three wishes.

31:20.962 --> 31:22.630
I robbed you of your life.

31:26.551 --> 31:29.596
So what if you know what "nostalgia" is?

31:30.513 --> 31:31.848
What about college?

31:32.932 --> 31:34.225
What about becoming a poet?

31:34.309 --> 31:35.685
What about the mainland?

31:37.020 --> 31:38.605
I can't give you everything.

31:39.230 --> 31:42.650
But one thing I will do for you,
no matter what.

31:43.151 --> 31:44.611
Come on.

31:44.694 --> 31:48.990
Can't you at least just say
you'll give me everything?

31:49.073 --> 31:52.702
Just tell me you will give me
the moon and the stars!

32:02.170 --> 32:04.172
You should've said no
when I was chasing you.

32:05.340 --> 32:07.050
You shouldn't have lived with me.

32:08.676 --> 32:13.389
Without you, I'd truly be an orphan
with no one in this world.

32:14.432 --> 32:16.142
Without Yang Gwan-sik,

32:16.225 --> 32:19.312
Oh Ae-sun couldn't have lived her life
as a coy girl.

32:20.063 --> 32:22.148
Should I teach that damn Mi-suk a lesson?

32:30.657 --> 32:34.035
Why are you aging on the outside
but not on the inside?

32:34.535 --> 32:37.622
How come your heart never changes?
It's so annoying.

32:45.296 --> 32:46.214
CHARMZONE CONTROL CREAM

32:46.297 --> 32:47.882
Lucky you, Hyeon-suk.

32:47.966 --> 32:51.719
My father-in-law
has never given me any cream.

32:54.305 --> 32:57.433
I've noticed
you haven't been dressing up much

32:58.017 --> 33:00.061
or wearing your hair all curly lately.

33:00.144 --> 33:01.938
Why don't you go get a perm?

33:02.021 --> 33:03.773
Perms are expensive.

33:07.819 --> 33:09.320
Read this for me.

33:09.404 --> 33:10.530
-What?
-This book.

33:10.613 --> 33:12.031
Right. Okay.

33:18.621 --> 33:21.249
Are you guys the only ones eating here?

33:21.332 --> 33:22.417
Come on.

33:22.500 --> 33:24.877
You know his father loves rolled omelets.

33:24.961 --> 33:27.797
How can you hide two-thirds of it?

33:27.880 --> 33:28.798
Goodness me.

33:30.800 --> 33:33.469
Tell Eun-myeong to come home
and join us when we eat

33:33.553 --> 33:35.763
instead of making us set the table twice.

33:35.847 --> 33:39.934
How much damn booze does he chug
to be knocked out until late morning?

33:42.478 --> 33:43.479
Mother, I'm hurt!

33:46.858 --> 33:48.109
I'm not going to eat.

33:58.578 --> 34:01.372
We have a daughter-in-law
who's just like our daughter.

34:53.633 --> 34:56.385
Why aren't you asleep?
We can put Che-il to bed.

35:01.140 --> 35:02.558
You guys should have it.

35:04.644 --> 35:05.728
You're sitting down?

35:06.437 --> 35:07.271
To drink too?

35:08.189 --> 35:10.441
You already know I like to drink.

35:11.859 --> 35:14.362
I was just looking for the hammer,

35:15.404 --> 35:18.116
but I found the acorns
my daughter-in-law squirreled away.

35:19.367 --> 35:22.245
Who buys a box of beer
for their daughter-in-law?

35:24.914 --> 35:26.958
It's not easy to live with strangers

35:27.041 --> 35:29.836
after eating your mom's cooking
for 20 years, is it?

35:31.254 --> 35:34.715
Honestly, I don't think living
with the in-laws is that difficult.

35:35.800 --> 35:36.634
Huh?

35:38.052 --> 35:39.512
I see.

35:40.555 --> 35:41.556
Actually…

35:45.726 --> 35:48.187
I'm so stressed out because of Eun-myeong.

35:50.314 --> 35:54.026
What about him?
Is that punk causing trouble again?

35:55.862 --> 35:59.157
Father, you don't know
what your son's been up to, do you?

36:10.209 --> 36:13.754
-Stop going to the ping-pong club.
-Who are you to tell me to go or not?

36:13.838 --> 36:18.176
People say Bu Sang-gil is the only one
playing in a mixed doubles team.

36:18.259 --> 36:22.221
Mixed doubles is a sport too.
Hyun Jung-hwa, Yoo Nam-kyu!

36:22.305 --> 36:23.848
Are you lonely or something?

36:25.808 --> 36:27.602
Lonely, my ass. Damn it.

36:28.811 --> 36:30.646
I'm the boss in my house!

36:31.564 --> 36:35.026
Come on, you don't have to act
like the boss all the time.

36:35.109 --> 36:36.110
Everyone avoids me.

36:41.866 --> 36:43.451
You can touch him, you know.

36:49.999 --> 36:52.168
Is this how
having a first grandchild feels?

36:53.085 --> 36:56.005
He's a spitting image of his dad.

36:56.088 --> 36:57.215
Of his mother.

37:00.968 --> 37:01.802
Of his mother.

37:02.386 --> 37:03.512
Fine.

37:03.596 --> 37:05.723
Let me know
if you want to see your grandson.

37:05.806 --> 37:07.308
I'll arrange it secretly for you.

37:09.185 --> 37:11.270
You want something from me, mister?

37:12.313 --> 37:13.147
"Mister"?

37:15.107 --> 37:16.943
You don't call me "Hey, you" anymore.

37:17.026 --> 37:19.445
What's the father of a daughter to do?

37:20.446 --> 37:21.572
I know how you feel.

37:22.949 --> 37:25.159
You think your son-in-law is a thief too?

37:26.118 --> 37:28.287
Wearing a love charity badge
makes you great?

37:28.371 --> 37:30.206
Try to show some love at home too.

37:30.289 --> 37:32.583
Then you won't go play ping-pong
on New Year.

37:44.053 --> 37:45.554
The tangerine field is yours.

37:47.265 --> 37:50.142
Accept it as payment
for cleaning up after me.

37:53.312 --> 37:55.189
While your father-in-law was alive…

37:57.441 --> 38:00.444
he never went to see
the camellia flowers in winter.

38:01.320 --> 38:04.490
When the canola flowers bloomed
in the west of Jeju,

38:04.991 --> 38:06.367
he'd go east to enjoy himself.

38:07.410 --> 38:09.954
When the camellia flowers bloomed
in the east,

38:10.037 --> 38:11.831
he'd go west to enjoy himself.

38:13.374 --> 38:15.042
That's what philandering is like.

38:15.710 --> 38:19.463
He knew other people also
saw his actions as shameful.

38:20.089 --> 38:24.468
He kept up those antics
until he kicked the bucket,

38:24.552 --> 38:26.804
but I didn't know how else to survive,

38:28.014 --> 38:29.515
so I just put up with it.

38:31.183 --> 38:34.520
I bottled it up, and in the end,
it took a toll on my health.

38:35.021 --> 38:36.230
Mother.

38:37.189 --> 38:38.858
Why are you doing this?

38:38.941 --> 38:40.651
What am I supposed to do?

38:41.152 --> 38:43.070
The tangerine field is yours.

38:44.322 --> 38:45.614
Do what you want with it.

38:53.622 --> 38:56.208
You're out looking
for a lucky strike again, aren't you?

38:56.917 --> 38:58.169
Seriously, that punk.

39:04.258 --> 39:08.262
Dong-jin's brother got out of the army,
so the boys are hanging out.

39:09.138 --> 39:10.348
I'll be home early.

39:13.851 --> 39:16.395
When do I ever drink milk?
I'll have diarrhea.

39:25.780 --> 39:27.948
We should stop him right away.

39:29.075 --> 39:32.244
If he causes trouble again,
there's nothing left for us to sell!

39:32.745 --> 39:35.164
All kids act up sometimes.

39:36.207 --> 39:38.667
But even a conch with spikes is valuable.

39:42.838 --> 39:44.965
Let's see. There.

39:45.049 --> 39:47.009
There you are. Good.

39:53.974 --> 39:54.809
You know,

39:55.684 --> 39:57.895
Hong-nam's big brother Hong-sik
opened a shop.

39:58.479 --> 40:02.316
Is this really the time to worry
about Hong-sik, Hong-nam's older brother?

40:02.858 --> 40:04.485
How late will you stay out?

40:07.113 --> 40:07.947
I don't want it.

40:08.614 --> 40:11.325
They're hot. These chestnuts are hot.

40:11.409 --> 40:13.244
Hey, I don't even like chestnuts.

40:13.744 --> 40:15.079
It's what you like.

40:19.667 --> 40:22.378
It's below zero today.
Don't stay out for too long.

40:48.195 --> 40:50.281
The words he used to tune out every night…

40:50.364 --> 40:52.741
Sticky rice cakes.

40:54.660 --> 40:56.871
Buckwheat jelly.

40:57.872 --> 41:02.001
…could not be shaken off
now that they were said by his own child.

41:02.084 --> 41:04.086
Sticky rice cakes!

41:06.964 --> 41:08.883
Buckwheat jelly!

41:14.763 --> 41:16.515
Sticky rice cakes!

41:18.225 --> 41:20.186
Buckwheat jelly!

41:21.228 --> 41:23.439
No one sells sticky rice cakes
here now, right?

41:24.315 --> 41:26.567
That's because Eun-myeong's doing it now.

41:27.902 --> 41:30.488
Even if he tries to get a job,
no one will hire him

41:30.571 --> 41:32.156
because he's been to jail.

41:32.239 --> 41:35.367
They all rejected him and called him
a deadbeat who steals money.

41:35.951 --> 41:39.830
He goes out in this cold weather
and wanders around for six or seven hours.

41:41.373 --> 41:42.458
I hate it.

41:43.459 --> 41:44.919
I hate it so much.

41:48.047 --> 41:51.717
Father, for the time being,
could you feed three more people?

41:52.801 --> 41:56.013
Our Che-il will eat almost less
than a half portion anyway.

41:57.348 --> 42:01.101
The other day, some drunkard
kicked the rice cake box.

42:01.602 --> 42:03.562
Someone called him up to the fifth floor,

42:03.646 --> 42:07.441
bought one portion of buckwheat jelly,
and asked him to take out their trash.

42:08.317 --> 42:10.986
He has to. He has to do something.

42:11.654 --> 42:13.405
He's the head of his household.

42:15.199 --> 42:17.159
Although that's what he told her…

42:17.243 --> 42:19.370
Just tell him he's doing well.

42:19.870 --> 42:20.955
Let him know.

42:23.832 --> 42:27.753
…a wall of Dad's heart
silently crumbled to pieces.

42:27.836 --> 42:30.047
How can I tell him he's doing well?

42:32.716 --> 42:35.511
Eun-myeong can't stand that kind of work.

42:35.594 --> 42:37.304
You know it too!

42:41.392 --> 42:42.685
Seriously, damn it!

42:43.644 --> 42:47.273
The number of suicides this past year
has reached record numbers.

42:47.356 --> 42:50.067
More heads of households
are taking their own lives

42:50.150 --> 42:52.152
due to job loss or financial struggles.

42:52.236 --> 42:53.988
Dad.

42:54.071 --> 42:57.741
Dad, please find Eun-myeong!

42:58.534 --> 43:00.619
If you don't find him, I'll take my life!

43:00.703 --> 43:02.329
I'll take my own life too!

43:02.413 --> 43:03.539
Where are you off again?

43:03.622 --> 43:04.665
He's on a boat.

43:04.748 --> 43:07.042
He's on a boat! Mi-suk saw him!

43:07.126 --> 43:08.502
The deep-sea fishing boat?

44:04.141 --> 44:05.392
Not the sea!

44:06.352 --> 44:08.228
Don't let him go out to sea!

44:10.064 --> 44:12.358
You'll bring Eun-myeong back, won't you?

44:12.941 --> 44:14.902
You'll bring him back, won't you?

44:19.406 --> 44:23.619
You know how much it is to fuel this boat?
Who are you to tell me to turn?

44:23.702 --> 44:25.579
Please turn the boat just this once!

44:26.080 --> 44:28.040
I'll pay for the gas as well!

44:28.749 --> 44:31.752
Time is money, too, isn't it?
Stop talking nonsense.

44:32.252 --> 44:34.755
For fuck's sake. Hang up now!

44:34.838 --> 44:36.632
This is Bu Sang-gil from Dodong-ri.

44:36.715 --> 44:38.592
Bu Sang-gil, my ass!

44:38.676 --> 44:40.010
Off to a shitty start.

44:40.094 --> 44:40.928
Double.

44:44.264 --> 44:45.974
I said double!

44:46.058 --> 44:47.059
Goddamn it!

44:47.142 --> 44:49.186
I said double, and you won't back down?

45:00.406 --> 45:02.491
Did you raise your son in a bubble?

45:02.574 --> 45:04.368
All he did was throw up.

45:04.451 --> 45:08.330
-Thank you.
-Were you on a passenger ferry or what?!

45:08.414 --> 45:10.624
What, you turned it back for free?

45:10.708 --> 45:12.459
Acting all goddamn generous.

45:12.543 --> 45:15.671
Why cause all this fuss
by letting a young boy get on the boat?

45:15.754 --> 45:16.755
Lower the price!

45:16.839 --> 45:18.382
Lower what price?

45:18.465 --> 45:20.259
-It's a done deal.
-Why, you…

45:20.342 --> 45:23.637
You have any idea how hard it is?
People die so easily.

45:23.721 --> 45:26.640
People drown, get caught in net haulers,
killed by ropes, lose hands.

45:26.724 --> 45:28.892
Everyone runs away from it!

45:29.685 --> 45:31.520
That's how hard it is!

45:32.104 --> 45:34.898
Why would you do something so deadly?

45:37.443 --> 45:38.527
If it's that hard,

45:39.611 --> 45:40.946
how did you manage?

45:48.996 --> 45:50.247
Let's go.

45:51.206 --> 45:53.959
-Mom can't go on if you go to sea.
-But you did it all!

45:54.042 --> 45:56.962
No matter how hard it was, you did it!

45:58.338 --> 46:00.466
Did someone say
you make a fortune on that boat?

46:00.549 --> 46:01.884
You after the lucky strike?

46:04.470 --> 46:06.138
I wanted to get your boat back.

46:08.599 --> 46:10.100
I don't need my boat back.

46:10.184 --> 46:13.103
Just don't get on a boat.
Do something else.

46:13.187 --> 46:16.148
If I do something else,
are you gonna buy everything again?

46:21.195 --> 46:25.324
You know what people said to me
when I was selling sticky rice cakes?

46:28.076 --> 46:29.328
Here are two more.

46:33.665 --> 46:34.625
I don't need change.

46:36.084 --> 46:37.419
-Sorry?
-Listen, kid.

46:37.503 --> 46:38.837
Be good to your father.

46:38.921 --> 46:40.172
Be good to him.

46:48.013 --> 46:49.056
I'm really not hungry.

46:50.224 --> 46:52.935
I don't really like
these kinds of emergency crops.

46:53.018 --> 46:55.562
You be good to your father. Be good.

47:01.985 --> 47:03.237
Four packets at this hour?

47:03.320 --> 47:04.905
I don't know. I was told to.

47:05.405 --> 47:06.240
By your mom?

47:06.323 --> 47:07.908
Oh, and I was told to tell you--

47:07.991 --> 47:09.284
To be good to my father?

47:13.914 --> 47:15.791
Are they paying for Christmas seals?

47:16.458 --> 47:18.544
Are my sticky rice cakes
like a charity badge?

47:19.962 --> 47:21.088
Seriously, damn it.

47:24.883 --> 47:26.426
How much is this? Damn it.

47:26.510 --> 47:32.057
Everyone buying rice cakes from me
tells me to be good to you!

47:32.558 --> 47:34.726
You planned this with my father-in-law!

47:34.810 --> 47:36.520
He gave everyone a 5,000-won bill.

47:36.603 --> 47:39.565
You both gave money to the neighbors
and the ping-pong club.

47:40.065 --> 47:42.442
Everyone bought my rice cakes
with my family's money.

47:43.151 --> 47:44.403
This is embarrassing.

47:46.947 --> 47:48.824
This is so embarrassing.

47:48.907 --> 47:50.117
Seriously,

47:51.243 --> 47:53.620
I was so embarrassed and sorry to you.

47:54.121 --> 47:56.957
Be good to your father,
or you'll deeply regret it.

47:58.125 --> 47:59.334
Don't worry about it!

48:04.590 --> 48:07.050
He needs to make money
to stay motivated in the cold.

48:07.551 --> 48:10.304
That way, he can shake off sleep
and have a reason to get up.

48:10.387 --> 48:11.263
-And--
-So?

48:11.346 --> 48:13.557
I should give money
to people in our building?

48:13.640 --> 48:14.850
To buy your son's food?

48:14.933 --> 48:17.686
You know all kinds of people around town.

48:18.353 --> 48:21.440
Who would complain
about getting free rice cakes?

48:22.107 --> 48:26.695
And whether you like it or not,
he's not just my son, is he?

48:31.325 --> 48:34.494
I can't believe I'm stuck
with a guy I can't stand. Damn it.

48:34.578 --> 48:37.164
Do you know when I started to dislike you?

48:38.373 --> 48:39.333
I don't want to know.

48:39.416 --> 48:40.709
I haven't liked you

48:40.792 --> 48:44.004
since the day you got on my boat
with your little floral lunch box.

48:45.213 --> 48:46.882
I didn't want to be on it either.

48:46.965 --> 48:48.717
Life is just the luck of the draw.

48:48.800 --> 48:52.095
I thought you were just living off luck
and enjoying life.

48:52.638 --> 48:56.975
Seeing you enjoy life because you happened
to meet a smart, frugal wife

48:57.851 --> 48:59.853
put me on the verge of getting angry.

49:00.979 --> 49:03.941
And you know,
I was set up on a date with her.

49:04.024 --> 49:07.277
Come on, don't be on the verge
of crossing the line.

49:08.278 --> 49:10.280
But it wasn't thanks to your wife.

49:12.032 --> 49:13.116
You're different.

49:22.417 --> 49:24.294
Turns out you were different from me.

49:24.378 --> 49:25.671
What's wrong with you?

49:25.754 --> 49:27.673
-Get off now.
-No, I won't.

49:27.756 --> 49:29.007
Get off already.

49:29.091 --> 49:30.050
No, I won't!

49:30.634 --> 49:32.928
Seriously, you are driving me nuts.

49:33.011 --> 49:34.388
Why do everything for me?

49:34.972 --> 49:36.932
You always tell me
to handle my own future.

49:37.015 --> 49:38.225
Hurry up, won't you?

49:39.267 --> 49:40.102
Your mom's crying.

49:41.144 --> 49:42.270
What am I, a baby?

49:42.771 --> 49:44.982
How long are you gonna clean up
after a grown-up?

49:45.065 --> 49:45.941
A grown-up?

49:47.192 --> 49:48.902
I'm not done raising you yet.

49:49.569 --> 49:52.114
Perhaps there are no grown-ups.

49:52.698 --> 49:55.993
Crazy bastards,
talking crap like "deadbeat" and "jail."

49:56.076 --> 49:58.245
If they talk shit, I won't let them be.

49:58.328 --> 50:00.580
I'll kill them. I will!

50:01.081 --> 50:03.000
It seems like everyone is a kid.

50:14.720 --> 50:19.516
Who told you to get on that boat?
You want me to die? Is that it?

50:20.976 --> 50:22.519
I heard you sold rice cakes too!

50:22.602 --> 50:24.521
Hyeon-suk told you everything, didn't she?

50:25.230 --> 50:26.273
Why didn't you tell me?

50:26.356 --> 50:28.025
Aren't you talking to me anymore?

50:28.108 --> 50:29.234
Are you still mad at me?

50:29.818 --> 50:31.069
Tell her you're sorry!

50:31.153 --> 50:33.238
Tell your mom you'll never do it again!

50:33.321 --> 50:34.322
No!

50:36.908 --> 50:39.036
It's all my fault!

50:42.039 --> 50:44.791
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

50:45.500 --> 50:49.463
I'll make you pork cutlets every day.

50:54.593 --> 50:56.470
Stop crying like that!

50:56.553 --> 51:00.182
Every time you do that,
the whole family becomes helpless.

51:23.497 --> 51:24.331
A deadbeat.

51:25.791 --> 51:26.625
A windbag.

51:27.793 --> 51:29.711
A thief who blew someone else's money.

51:29.795 --> 51:33.215
You know why I hired you
even though no one else would?

51:33.715 --> 51:36.301
I don't know
if I should say this about a person.

51:36.384 --> 51:39.596
I'm hiring you because you're the son
of a premium horse.

51:40.097 --> 51:42.557
At races,
premium horses can cost millions.

51:43.391 --> 51:45.685
But their offspring
are even more expensive.

51:45.769 --> 51:47.521
They're worth millions without racing.

51:47.604 --> 51:50.941
Cows, horses, and people
all have different tiers.

51:52.025 --> 51:55.445
People look down on a diligent person
for being old-fashioned these days.

51:56.196 --> 51:58.406
But your father's level of diligence
is something

51:58.490 --> 52:00.534
that no one should dare to look down on.

52:00.617 --> 52:03.245
Is everyone here itching to nag me
whenever they see me?

52:03.328 --> 52:05.330
I got stopped three times on my way here.

52:05.413 --> 52:07.457
So why did you try to run a business?

52:07.541 --> 52:10.085
You soured it,
so now your parents in their fifties--

52:10.168 --> 52:12.212
I soured it? No, the IMF crisis did.

52:15.465 --> 52:17.551
The new millennium is almost upon us.

52:18.176 --> 52:20.053
Let's all shout together!

52:20.137 --> 52:24.349
Ten! Nine! Eight! Seven!

52:24.432 --> 52:27.769
The coming age mercilessly drove us
out the door without fail.

52:27.853 --> 52:30.188
Four! Three!

52:30.272 --> 52:31.690
Two! One!

52:35.527 --> 52:37.904
At last, the new millennium has arrived!

52:43.577 --> 52:45.453
It's the 2000s now.

52:45.537 --> 52:46.538
Can you believe it?

52:46.621 --> 52:50.208
We've been together
since the 1950s, right?

52:55.338 --> 52:59.718
I think something big will happen
in our family in the new millennium.

53:00.260 --> 53:01.261
Why is that?

53:04.764 --> 53:06.558
Because we hit rock bottom.

53:08.518 --> 53:11.646
It's not easy for all four family members
to lose their jobs, is it?

53:13.356 --> 53:14.441
Are you happy?

53:15.192 --> 53:17.027
You laugh so easily at silly things.

53:18.987 --> 53:22.616
Even a cat shrinks as small as it can
before it springs up.

53:23.408 --> 53:26.536
I think something is about to "Ready, go!"

53:28.288 --> 53:32.083
It'll help you develop a lean physique
and toned muscles.

53:33.710 --> 53:34.836
While almost silent,

53:34.920 --> 53:38.048
it also minimizes joint impact
with its elliptical rotation,

53:38.131 --> 53:41.176
making it a fun workout
for people of all ages and genders.

53:42.177 --> 53:44.638
Four exercise machines in one, Cyclone!

53:45.513 --> 53:46.806
The secret to our stock?

53:46.890 --> 53:51.061
In our family, not even our son,
let alone his wife, knows.

53:52.729 --> 53:54.022
Hey, it's Natasha!

53:54.105 --> 53:56.524
Natasha! It's the Natasha noodles again!

54:00.528 --> 54:04.199
I wonder if Song Bu-seon
is handling the noodles well.

54:04.282 --> 54:09.704
Why should my past
become the subject of your jokes?

54:10.330 --> 54:11.248
That's hot.

54:11.331 --> 54:16.503
Bu-seon's noodles do look really good.
I feel like I'm tasting them by looking.

54:17.295 --> 54:18.588
Shall I cook some ramyeon?

54:19.589 --> 54:20.590
One last time?

54:21.091 --> 54:22.092
-Babe.
-Yeah?

54:22.717 --> 54:26.846
Don't you think a time will come
when we can do everything with our eyes?

54:27.555 --> 54:32.185
We could get to places, eat, learn,
and exercise just with our eyes.

54:39.943 --> 54:40.777
What is it?

54:40.860 --> 54:43.488
Are you coming up
with another business idea?

54:44.072 --> 54:46.825
Right now, everyone is broke
because of the IMF crisis.

54:48.994 --> 54:51.413
When everyone's struggling together,

54:52.289 --> 54:54.916
shouldn't there be
a redistribution of wealth?

54:57.127 --> 55:00.880
Shouldn't I also try to grab an ace
at a time like this?

55:01.506 --> 55:02.590
You're right.

55:02.674 --> 55:06.344
Heroes rarely emerge
in peaceful and prosperous times.

55:07.846 --> 55:08.680
You got this!

55:16.187 --> 55:17.522
I've gotta have some ramyeon.

55:33.997 --> 55:37.417
Will you be swept by the waves?
Or will you ride the waves?

55:39.336 --> 55:41.379
…and straight to the catcher. He's out!

55:41.463 --> 55:42.881
Game over!

55:43.798 --> 55:46.760
That was up to the runner.

55:48.553 --> 55:52.474
I passed, thanks to the IMF crisis!

55:52.557 --> 55:54.934
The exam used to be held
once every two years.

55:55.018 --> 55:58.063
But now, it's held every year
because of the IMF crisis!

55:58.563 --> 56:00.523
Yes!

56:00.607 --> 56:02.984
I checked the answers for myself!

56:03.693 --> 56:05.403
I won!

56:05.904 --> 56:07.405
I really won!

56:09.574 --> 56:10.992
But, Mom,

56:11.076 --> 56:14.120
why do you keep saying you won
instead of saying you passed?

56:14.204 --> 56:15.622
It makes me feel uneasy.

56:16.581 --> 56:20.043
It felt amazing the moment I hit it.

56:20.126 --> 56:21.503
I saw the ball get past

56:22.212 --> 56:24.214
and ran to second base.

56:24.297 --> 56:27.133
Words can't describe
how exhilarating that was.

56:27.717 --> 56:29.886
I saw liberation when I was 13,

56:29.969 --> 56:32.972
and now I get to see
"Long live Korea" once again.

56:33.056 --> 56:37.560
I wonder if Lee Seung-yuop
wanted to be a baseball player as a child.

56:38.561 --> 56:43.650
You'd have no regrets if you could win
a medal in the dream you pursued.

56:44.150 --> 56:45.777
You have many regrets?

56:45.860 --> 56:47.612
What regrets could you have?

56:47.695 --> 56:50.281
Your life has been
like a precious jewel all along.

56:50.365 --> 56:53.368
Your husband still thinks
you can't carry a bag of rice.

56:55.537 --> 56:56.413
You're right.

56:56.913 --> 57:00.542
If I lived your life,
I would have written poems.

57:01.251 --> 57:02.836
I'd have written something.

57:02.919 --> 57:06.005
The entire island knew
you wanted to be a poet.

57:06.089 --> 57:07.465
So why don't you write?

57:08.299 --> 57:11.177
Is there an age limit to writing poetry?

57:11.261 --> 57:14.806
If all the literary girls became poets,

57:16.099 --> 57:18.101
everyone would be one.

57:18.685 --> 57:20.478
How can you get by without writing?

57:20.979 --> 57:23.022
If I had lived Oh Ae-sun's life,

57:23.523 --> 57:27.193
I would've written a thousand poems
just to brag about my life.

57:33.741 --> 57:35.702
2000
HOUSEHOLD ACCOUNT BOOK

57:46.463 --> 57:47.964
When one door closes,

57:48.465 --> 57:51.050
another is bound to creak open.

58:08.610 --> 58:11.070
M.F.L.

58:22.499 --> 58:25.335
A first page as white
as freshly fallen snow unfolds.

58:48.149 --> 58:52.237
Don't you know the American saying,
"High risk, high return"?

58:53.655 --> 58:55.615
Now that area in Jeju is going to boom.

58:55.698 --> 59:00.912
The stationary ship's horn echoed
like a pulsing heartbeat again.

59:00.995 --> 59:03.498
Captain Yang, with this,
your wife's struggles end,

59:03.998 --> 59:05.917
and you fulfill a father's duties.

59:06.417 --> 59:08.586
I heard your daughter
started a business too.

59:09.087 --> 59:10.880
She must have some backup, right?

59:12.215 --> 59:14.467
It takes one lucky strike
to be a good father.

59:15.426 --> 59:17.387
In the first winter of the new millennium,

59:18.096 --> 59:19.430
we were each getting ready

59:20.765 --> 59:22.725
to make a big move.

59:24.185 --> 59:27.188
It's a "Ready, go" moment for me too.

59:27.272 --> 59:28.815
Ready, go.

59:49.669 --> 59:52.505
SPREAD YOUR WINGS AND FLY

01:02:37.628 --> 01:02:42.925
"IF YOU CAN'T, JUST BACK DOWN.
WE'RE ALWAYS HERE FOR YOU."

01:02:50.057 --> 01:02:52.351
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
